From cee76279d72416f5f38783b5578b0b25664e0ed8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 16:20:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: mfd: syscon: add the MT8173 MCUCFG

MT8173 has an MCUCFG block at 0x10200000 that has never been described. Its
siblings mt2712 and mt8183 list theirs in clock/mediatek,syscon.yaml, but
that binding is for clock providers -- it requires #clock-cells -- and on
MT8173 nothing in the block is exposed as a clock. It is used purely as a
syscon, the way mediatek,mt8173-pctl-a-syscfg already is, so it belongs in
this list.

The consumer is MT8173 CPU bring-up, which needs CA15L_MISCDBG in this
block to deassert ACINACTM on the A72 cluster before the second cluster's
cores can join. Without a compatible in some schema the node matches
nothing at all and dtbs_check rejects the board.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml
index e22867088..764303ea1 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml
@@ -90,6 +90,7 @@ select:
           - mediatek,mt7988-topmisc
           - mediatek,mt8135-pctl-a-syscfg
           - mediatek,mt8135-pctl-b-syscfg
+          - mediatek,mt8173-mcucfg
           - mediatek,mt8173-pctl-a-syscfg
           - mediatek,mt8365-syscfg
           - microchip,lan966x-cpu-syscon
@@ -203,6 +204,7 @@ properties:
               - mediatek,mt7988-topmisc
               - mediatek,mt8135-pctl-a-syscfg
               - mediatek,mt8135-pctl-b-syscfg
+              - mediatek,mt8173-mcucfg
               - mediatek,mt8173-pctl-a-syscfg
               - mediatek,mt8365-infracfg-nao
               - mediatek,mt8365-syscfg
